  "summary": "EFF reposts an op-ed urging San Jose to terminate its Flock ALPR program, citing risks to immigrants from ICE access to ALPR data and noting San Jose police conduct hundreds of warrantless ALPR searches daily. It contrasts San Jose with nearby jurisdictions (Mountain View, Los Altos Hills, Santa Cruz, East Palo Alto, Santa Clara County) that have shut off or are reconsidering Flock.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In a little over a year, San Jose police logged more than 261,000 ALPR searches, or nearly 700 searches a day, all without a warrant.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "California law prohibits local police from disclosing ALPR data to out-of-state or federal agencies. But at least 75 California police agencies were sharing these records out-of-state as recently as 2023.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "A better solution is to simply turn these cameras off.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
